// Discovery has three activities and none of them is about a person.
//
//     event-storm       breadth — the whole timeline, shallow
//     notional-arch.    what the capabilities are to each other
//     walkthrough       depth — one path, all the way down
//
// Every one is about the SYSTEM. The record can say what a capability owns, what a slice
// claims, what a rule refuses — and cannot say who any of it is for.
//
// `needed-by="reader"` has been on every read model since the storm was written. It is a
// label with nothing behind it: no statement of who a reader is, what they came for, what
// they do not care about, or how they would know they got it. So a view can be correctly
// labelled and still speak to nobody, and `useful-alone` — the field that literally says
// "what you get" — never says who "you" is.
//
// The persona analysis that produced this slice was done in somebody's head and delivered as
// prose. Nothing holds it, nothing checks it, and the next agent will do it again. That is
// S7 with the product's own users as the thing being re-derived.

thin-slice "TS.260821.15" {
    slug "know-who-this-is-for"
    title "Hold who the product is for, so value is claimed from their side"
    kind "command"
    realizes "CAP.delivery-record"
    from-storm "ES.260819.01"

    command "check"
    actor "whoever is running discovery, before any capability is named"
    produces-event "PersonaDeclared" "ValueUnattributed"
    needs-read-model "the-problem-as-it-stands"

    trigger "somebody asks who this is for and the answer is in a person's head"
    outcome "the record holds each persona, and every claim of value names whose value it is"

    scenario #"""
        Given a frame with symptoms and a set of read models labelled `needed-by`
        When a persona is declared — who they are, what they came for, what they do not care
             about, and how they judge whether they got it
        Then `needed-by` names something the record holds, and a slice's `useful-alone` says
             whose — because value is not a property of a change, it is a judgement somebody
             makes, and a record that states the change without the judge has recorded half of it.
        """#

    step "1" does="`persona` is a kind: who they are, what they came for, what they do not care about, and what would make them say it worked"
    step "1b" does="ONE persona is named before framing — the primary one, who the product is for. The rest emerge from the work and are added as they are found"
    step "2" does="`needed-by` references it. A view for `reader` where no persona is named `reader` goes dangling, the way every other unresolved edge does"
    step "3" does="a slice's `useful-alone` names whose. `what you get if this ships and nothing after it does` has always had an unstated subject"
    step "4" does="a symptom names who feels it. S1 through S7 describe things that are wrong for SOMEBODY, and the frame has never said who"
    step "5" does="discovery gains the activity. Storm, architecture and walkthrough are all about the system; naming the person comes before any of them"

    excludes "enumerating every persona upfront. The primary one is knowable before framing — it \
        is the reason discovery is happening at all — and the rest are discovered. A week spent \
        writing personas for people nobody has met is the artifact this frame distrusts, produced \
        earlier"
    excludes "market segments, demographics, or anything a persona document usually carries. \
        What is needed here is what a reader came for and how they judge it — the rest is \
        marketing research and the record cannot check a word of it"
    excludes "one persona per role in the workflow. `reviewer` and `working-agent` are ROLES, \
        which TS.260821.08 already made a kind. A role is what you may attest; a persona is what \
        you came for, and one person occupies several roles across a week"
    excludes "refusing a slice that names no persona. Half this record predates the kind, and a \
        rule that fails closed on the day it lands names every slice ever cut — reported first, \
        the way every enforcement in this frame has had to earn its severity"

    layer "doctrine"    reaches="discovery names the person before it names the system, and the skill says what a persona must answer to be one"
    layer "enforcement" reaches="needed-by references persona; a claim of value naming no persona is reported"
    layer "docs"        reaches="`who is this for` is answerable from the record, and the published set can be ordered by a real reader instead of a label"

    claim "C5" text="one primary persona is required and the rest are not" \
        settled-by="a test asserting a record with no persona at all is reported, and one with a single primary persona is clean — emergence is the normal case, not a shortfall"
    claim "C6" text="an emergent persona names what surfaced it" \
        settled-by="a test asserting a persona declared as emergent with no `found-by` is refused, and that `found-by` follows to a finding, a walkthrough or a slice the record holds — discovered means discovered BY something"
    claim "C1" text="a persona is a record: who, what they came for, what they do not care about, how they judge it" \
        settled-by="praxis check over declared personas, and a test that one missing `judges-by` is refused — a persona nobody can be wrong about is a description, not a persona"
    claim "C2" text="needed-by names a persona the record holds, or it dangles" \
        settled-by="a test declaring a view needed-by a persona nothing declares, asserting dangling-relationship refuses it without a second rule"
    claim "C3" text="a claim of value names whose value it is" \
        settled-by="a test asserting a slice whose useful-alone names no persona is REPORTED, and that the report is not a refusal because half the record predates the kind"
    claim "C4" text="a symptom names who feels it" \
        settled-by="a test asserting a symptom with no `felt-by` is reported, and the frame amended so S1 through S7 each name somebody"

    depends-on "TS.260821.01 — a kind is declared on the schema before the record can hold one"

    useful-alone "for whoever runs discovery: `who is this for` stops being answered from memory. \
        The persona analysis that cut this slice took an afternoon, produced six paragraphs of \
        prose, and left nothing behind that the next agent can check or contradict"

    attacks "S7"

    cut-from "the maintainer, on reading the published set as two personas" \
        note="the prompt was a UCD review of the documents. The finding underneath it is that \
            discovery never produced a user — so the review had to invent the personas in order \
            to run, and inventing them again next time is guaranteed"

    principle-note "this frame computes fidelity from the record and has never held the one fact \
        every other fact is FOR. A capability is a permanent doing the system must have — for \
        whom? A claim is what a slice makes true — worth what, to whom? The vocabulary is complete \
        about the system and silent about the person, which is why every judgement about value in \
        this repository has been made in prose by whoever happened to be reading"

    proves "who the product is for is a fact the record holds, and value is claimed from their side"
    does-not-prove "that the personas are RIGHT. It makes them checkable and contradictable, which \
        is the most a record can do — a wrong persona stated is worth more than a right one assumed"
}
